	 b:glossaryEntry="breed of heavy-coated Arctic sled dog"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101619584"
	 b:glossaryEntry="breed of sled dog developed in Alaska"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101619706">
	<b:glossaryEntry>breed of sled dog developed in northeastern Siberia; they resemble the larger Alaskan malamutes</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101619862">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a large breed having a smooth white coat with black or brown spots; originated in Dalmatia</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620053"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a brown-spotted dalmatian"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620148">
	<b:glossaryEntry>European breed of small dog resembling a terrier with dark wiry hair and a tufted muzzle</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620327">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small smooth-haired breed of African origin having a tightly curled tail and the inability to bark</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620479">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small compact smooth-coated breed of Asiatic origin having a tightly curled tail and broad flat wrinkled muzzle</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620650">
	<b:glossaryEntry>breed of very large heavy usually black dogs developed in Newfoundland; highly intelligent and vigorous swimmers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620821">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bred of large heavy-coated white dogs resembling the Newfoundland</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101620947">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various stocky heavy-coated breeds of dogs native to northern regions having pointed muzzles and erect ears with a curled furry tail</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101621210"
	 b:glossaryEntry="Siberian breed of white or cream dog of the spitz family"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101621331">
	<b:glossaryEntry>breed of very small compact long-haired dogs of the spitz type</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101621450">
	<b:glossaryEntry>breed of thick-coated medium-sized dogs with fluffy curled tails and distinctive blue-black tongues; believed to have originated in north China</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101621656">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a spitz-type dog having a shaggy grayish coat and tightly curled tail originating in Holland</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101621803">
	<b:glossaryEntry>breed of various very small compact wiry-coated dogs of Belgian origin having a short bearded muzzle</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101622012"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a variety of Brussels_griffon having a short smooth coat"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101622132">
	<b:glossaryEntry>either of two Welsh breeds of long-bodied short-legged dogs with erect ears and a fox-like head</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101622329">
	<b:glossaryEntry>the smaller and straight-legged variety of corgi having pointed ears and a short tail</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101622492">
	<b:glossaryEntry>slightly bow-legged variety of corgi having rounded ears and a long tail</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101622642">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an intelligent dog with a heavy curly solid-colored coat that is usually clipped; an old breed sometimes trained as sporting dogs or as performing dogs</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101622931"
	 b:glossaryEntry="the smallest poodle"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623007"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a small poodle"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623084"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a medium-sized poodle"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623167"
	 b:glossaryEntry="the largest poodle"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623244"
	 b:glossaryEntry="any of an old breed of small nearly hairless dogs of Mexico"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623366">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various predatory carnivorous canine mammals of North America and Eurasia that usually hunt in packs</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623615">
	<b:glossaryEntry>brindled gray wolf of forested northern regions of North America</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623763">
	<b:glossaryEntry>wolf of arctic North America having white fur and a black-tipped tail</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101623927"
	 b:glossaryEntry="reddish-gray wolf of southwestern North America"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101624070"
	 b:glossaryEntry="small wolf native to western North America"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101624227"
	 b:glossaryEntry="offspring of a coyote and a dog"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101624311">
	<b:glossaryEntry>Old World nocturnal canine mammal closely related to the dog; smaller than a wolf; sometimes hunts in a pack but usually singly or as a member of a pair</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101624550">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various undomesticated mammals of the family Canidae that are thought to resemble domestic dogs as distinguished from jackals or wolves</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101624856"
	 b:glossaryEntry="wolflike yellowish-brown wild dog of Australia"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101624990"
	 b:glossaryEntry="Asiatic wild dog"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625128">
	<b:glossaryEntry>fierce wild dog of the forests of central and southeast Asia that hunts in packs</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625294"
	 b:glossaryEntry="crab-eating dog"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625400"
	 b:glossaryEntry="wild dog of northern South America"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625537"
	 b:glossaryEntry="raccoon dogs"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625665">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small wild dog of eastern Asia having facial markings like those of a raccoon</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625845"
	 b:glossaryEntry="African hunting dog"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101625953">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a powerful doglike mammal of South and East Africa that hunts in large packs; now rare in settled area</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101626168"
	 b:glossaryEntry="hyenas"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101626344">
	<b:glossaryEntry>doglike nocturnal mammal of Africa and southern Asia that feeds chiefly on carrion</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101626578"
	 b:glossaryEntry="type genus of the Hyaenidae"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101626721"
	 b:glossaryEntry="of northern Africa and Arabia and India"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101626855"
	 b:glossaryEntry="of southern Africa"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101626981"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a genus of Hyaenidae"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101627109"
	 b:glossaryEntry="African hyena noted for its distinctive howl"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101627267"
	 b:glossaryEntry="aardwolf"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101627385">
	<b:glossaryEntry>striped mammal of southeast Africa that feeds chiefly on insects</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101627543">
	<b:glossaryEntry>alert carnivorous mammal with pointed muzzle and ears and a bushy tail; most are predators that do not hunt in packs</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101627835">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a conventional name for a fox used in tales following usage in the old epic "Reynard the Fox"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101627982"
	 b:glossaryEntry="foxes"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101628150">
	<b:glossaryEntry>the common Old World fox; having reddish-brown fur; commonly considered a single circumpolar species</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101628375"
	 b:glossaryEntry="red fox in the color phase when its pelt is mostly black"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101628487">
	<b:glossaryEntry>red fox in the color phase when its pelt is tipped with white</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101628605">
	<b:glossaryEntry>New World fox; often considered the same species las the Old World fox</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101628763"
	 b:glossaryEntry="small gray fox of the plains of western North America"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101628918">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small gray fox of southwestern United States; may be a subspecies of Vulpes velox</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101629090"
	 b:glossaryEntry="arctic foxes"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101629208">
	<b:glossaryEntry>thickly-furred fox of Arctic regions; brownish in summer and white in winter</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101629407"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a variety of arctic_fox having a pale gray winter coat"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101629516"
	 b:glossaryEntry="gray foxes"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101629634">
	<b:glossaryEntry>dark gray American fox; from Central America through southern United States</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
