	<b:glossaryEntry>intelligent somewhat arboreal ape of equatorial African forests</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101976248">
	<b:glossaryEntry>masked or pale-faced chimpanzees of western Africa; distantly related to the eastern and central chimpanzees; possibly a distinct species</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101976474">
	<b:glossaryEntry>long-haired chimpanzees of east-central Africa including the Gombe-Kasakela population; closely related to the central chimpanzees</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101976702">
	<b:glossaryEntry>black-faced chimpanzees of central Africa; closely related to eastern chimpanzees</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101976878">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small chimpanzee of swamp forests in Zaire; a threatened species</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;101977048">
	<b:glossaryEntry>used in some classifications for the lesser apes (gibbons and siamangs); sometimes considered a subfamily of Pongidae</b:glossaryEntry>
