	<b:glossaryEntry>the sacred city of Lamaism; known as the Forbidden City for its former inaccessibility and hostility to strangers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106512746">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a republic in southeastern Asia including more than 13,000 islands; freed from Dutch control in 1949; the principal oil producer in the Far East and Pacific regions</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106513176">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an island in Indonesia S of Borneo; one of the world''s most densely populated regions</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106513368">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an island in Indonesia east of Java; striking volcanic scenery; culture is known for elaborate dances and rituals and for handicrafts</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106513590"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a mountainous island in western Indonesia"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106513723"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a mountainous island in eastern Indonesia"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106513848"
	 b:glossaryEntry="the part of Indonesia on the S of the island of Borneo"/>
