<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106515761">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an ancient city that was the capital of the Persian Empire; now in ruins</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106515909">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a republic in the Middle East; the ancient civilization of Mesopotamia was in the area now known as Iraq</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106516233">
	<b:glossaryEntry>capital and largest city of Iraq; located on the Tigris River; "Baghdad is one of the great cities of the Moslem world"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106516452">
	<b:glossaryEntry>the former name for the geographical area of the eastern Mediterranean that is now occupied by Lebanon and Syria and Israel</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106516647">
	<b:glossaryEntry>the ancient kingdom of Phillip II and Alexander the Great in the southeastern Balkans that is now divided among Greece and Bulgaria and the former Yugoslavia</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106516946">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a region and ancient country in the east of the Balkan Peninsula north of the Aegean Sea; colonized by ancient Greeks; later a Roman province; now divided between Greece and Turkey</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106517217">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a city in northwestern Turkey; a Thracian town that was rebuilt and renamed by the Roman emperor Hadrian</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106517421">
	<b:glossaryEntry>the land between the Tigris and Euphrates; site of several ancient civilizations</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106517616">
	<b:glossaryEntry>the chief city of ancient Mesopotamia and capitol of the ancient kingdom of Babylonia</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;106517793">
