</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108122730">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an old cottage garden plant of southeastern Europe widely cultivated for its attractive white woolly foliage and showy crimson flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108122994">
	<b:glossaryEntry>mostly perennial herbs of northern hemisphere often with mat-forming habit; most often placed in genus Arenaria: sandworts</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108123209">
	<b:glossaryEntry>low-growing herbs widely distributed in temperate and arctic northern hemisphere: sandworts; distinguished from members of the genus Arenaria mainly by having 4- rather than 5-petaled flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108123533">
	<b:glossaryEntry>low-growing herb having clusters of small white-flowers 4-petaled flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108123705">
	<b:glossaryEntry>loosely matted plant with mosslike foliage studded with tiny starry 4-petaled white blossoms; mountains of central and southern Europe</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108123933">
	<b:glossaryEntry>low-growing annual or perennial herbs or woody plants; whitlowworts</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108124114">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various low-growing tufted plants of the genus Paronychia having tiny greenish flowers and usually whorled leaves; widespread throughout warm regions of both Old and New Worlds; formerly thought to cure whitlows (suppurative infections around a fingernail)</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108124454">
	<b:glossaryEntry>perennial tussock-forming rock plants; of Pyrenees and mountains of northern Spain; similar to and sometimes placed in genus Lychnis</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108124683">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small low-growing annual or perennial herbs of temperate and cool regions</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108124862">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various low-growing plants of the genus Sagina having small spherical flowers resembling pearls</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108125051"
	 b:glossaryEntry="mostly perennial Old World herbs"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108125195">
	<b:glossaryEntry>plant of European origin having pink or white flowers and leaves yielding a detergent when bruised</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108125435"
	 b:glossaryEntry="small genus of Old World weedy prostrate annuals: knawel"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108125607">
