</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108226116">
	<b:glossaryEntry>small tender herb grown for its fluffy brushlike blue to lavender blooms</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108226274">
	<b:glossaryEntry>herbs of Mediterranean to central Asia cultivated for their flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108226451">
	<b:glossaryEntry>Asian plant widely grown for its sweetly fragrant pink flowers; sometimes placed in genus Centaurea</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108226669">
	<b:glossaryEntry>comprising the ragweeds; in some classification considered the type genus of a separate family Ambrosiaceae</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108226875">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in some classifications considered a separate family comprising a subgroup of the Compositae including the ragweeds</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108227090">
