	<b:glossaryEntry>small genus of North American herbs often included in genus Eriophyllum</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108231706">
	<b:glossaryEntry>tiny gray woolly tufted annual with small golden-eyllow flower heads; southeastern California to northwestern Arizona and southwestern Utah; sometimes placed in genus Eriophyllum</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108232022"
	 b:glossaryEntry="burdock"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108232137">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of several erect biennial herbs of temperate Eurasia having stout taproots and producing burs</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108232353">
