	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various plants of the genus Halenia having flowers with spurred lobes</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108602211">
	<b:glossaryEntry>genus of smooth slender North American herbs with showy flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108602373">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various plants of the genus Sabbatia having usually pink cymose flowers; occur from acid bogs to brackish marshes</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108602621"
	 b:glossaryEntry="pink-flowered marsh plant of the eastern United States"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108602787"
	 b:glossaryEntry="pink-flowered marsh plant of the eastern United States"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108602939"
	 b:glossaryEntry="prairie herb with solitary lilac-colored flowers"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108603085">
	<b:glossaryEntry>genus of herbs of mountains of North America and Eurasia and Africa</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108603260">
	<b:glossaryEntry>perennial of damp places in mountains of Eurasia and North America having dull-colored blue or violet flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108603467">
	<b:glossaryEntry>trees and shrubs having berries or drupes or capsules as fruits; sometimes placed in the order Oleales: olive; ash; jasmine; privet; lilac</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
