	<b:glossaryEntry>California herb with white conic or bell-shaped flowers usually green-tinged</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108754732">
	<b:glossaryEntry>Eurasian checkered lily with pendant flowers usually veined and checkered with purple or maroon on a pale ground and shaped like the bells carried by lepers in medieval times; widely grown as an ornamental</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;108755085">
