	<b:glossaryEntry>a genus of dicotyledonous trees belonging to the family Lepidobotryaceae</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109001341">
	<b:glossaryEntry>African tree often classified in other families; similar to the Costa Rican caracolito in wood structure as well as in fruit and flowers and leaves and seeds</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109001576">
	<b:glossaryEntry>new (1993) genus of trees of Central America now recognized as similar to those of genus Lepidobotrys</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109001799">
	<b:glossaryEntry>large Costa Rican mahogonylike tree having light-colored wood suitable for cabinetry; similar to the African lepidobotrys in wood structure as well as in fruit and flowers and leaves and seeds; often classified in other families</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109002131">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a family of widely distributed herbs of the order Geraniales; have compound leaves and pentamerous flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109002394">
	<b:glossaryEntry>type genus of the Oxalidaceae; large genus of plants having leaves that resemble clover and variously colored flowers usually clustered in umbels</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109002636"
	 b:glossaryEntry="any plant or flower of the genus Oxalis"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109002878">
	<b:glossaryEntry>Eurasian plant with heart-shaped trifoliate leaves and white pink- or purple-veined flowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109003080"
	 b:glossaryEntry="South African bulbous wood sorrel with showy yellow flowers"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109003254"
	 b:glossaryEntry="creeping much-branched mat-forming weed; cosmopolitan"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109003413"
	 b:glossaryEntry="short-stemmed South African plant with bluish flowers"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;109003553">
