	<b:glossaryEntry>any of several fat-soluble vitamins essential for normal vision; prevents night blindness or inflammation or dryness of the eyes</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110825223">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an unsaturated alcohol that occurs in marine fish-liver oils and is synthesized biologically from carotene</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110825396">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a viscous alcohol that is less active in mammals than is vitamin A1</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110825537">
	<b:glossaryEntry>an orange isomer of an unsaturated hydrocarbon found in many plants; is converted into vitamin A in the liver</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110825726">
	<b:glossaryEntry>originally thought to be a single vitamin but now separated into several B vitamins</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110826113">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a B vitamin that prevents beriberi; maintains appetite and growth</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110826288"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a B vitamin that is used to treat pernicious anemia"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110826457"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a B vitamin that prevents skin lesions and weight loss"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110826634">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a B vitamin that is essential for metabolism of amino acids and starch</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110826811">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a B vitamin that is essential for cell growth and reproduction</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827024">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a B vitamin essential for the normal function of the nervous system and the gastrointestinal tract</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827192"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a fat-soluble vitamin that prevents rickets"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827362">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a fat-soluble vitamin that is essential for normal reproduction; an important antioxidant that neutralizes free radicals in the body</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827567"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a B vitamin that aids in body growth"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827668"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a fat-soluble vitamin that helps clot blood"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827820"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a form of vitamin K"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110827927"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a form of vitamin K"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828015">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a vitamin that maintains the resistance of cell and capillary walls to permeation</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828176">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a vitamin found in fresh fruits (especially citrus fruits) and vegetables; prevents scurvy</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828338">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(H2SO4) a highly corrosive acid made from sulfur dioxide; widely used in the chemical industry</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828573">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a volatile substance; a substance that changes readily from solid or liquid to a vapor; "it was heated to evaporate the volatiles"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828758"
	 b:glossaryEntry="a decorative paper for the walls of rooms"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828855"
	 b:glossaryEntry="the water present in hydrated compounds"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110828986">
	<b:glossaryEntry>any of various substances of either mineral origin or plant or animal origin; they are solid at normal temperatures and insoluble in water</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
