	<b:glossaryEntry>paper that has been waterproofed by treatment with wax of paraffin</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110831243">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a substance capable of reducing the surface tension of a liquid in which it is dissolved</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110831463">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a surface-active chemical widely used in industry and laundering</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;110831619">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a substance added to soaps or detergents to increase their cleansing action</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
