	<b:glossaryEntry>stay the same; remain in a certain state; "The dress remained wet after repeated attempts to dry it"; "rest assured"; "stay alone"; "He remained unmoved by her tears"; "The bad weather continued for another week"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200078842">
	<b:glossaryEntry>exist over a prolonged period of time; "The bad weather continued for two more weeks"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079065">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[keep informed; "He kept up on his country''s foreign policies"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079239">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[maintain the same position; wait it out; "Let''s not make a decision--let''s sit tight"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079391"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become distinct"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079477"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become different during development; of cells"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079593"
	 b:glossaryEntry='undergo mutation; "cells mutate"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079689"
	 b:glossaryEntry="cause to undergo mutation; of cells"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079788"
	 b:glossaryEntry="change venous blood into arterial blood"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200079910">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[give certain properties to something; "get someone mad"; "She made us look silly"; "He made a fool of himself at the meeting"; "Don''t make this into a big deal"; "This invention will make you a famous physicist"; "Make yourself clear"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200080274"
	 b:glossaryEntry='cause to become; "The shot rendered her immobile"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200080395">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to move; cause to be in a certain position or condition: "He got his squad on the ball"; "This let me in for a big surprise"; "He got a girl into trouble"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200080645"
	 b:glossaryEntry='undergo; "The stocks had a fast run-up"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200080777"
	 b:glossaryEntry='do something in turns; "We take turns on the night shift"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200080914">
	<b:glossaryEntry>go back and forth; swing back and forth between two states or conditions</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081068"
	 b:glossaryEntry="reverse, as of direction or attitude"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081221"
	 b:glossaryEntry="cause to change places, as of parts, for example"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081366">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to roast or calcine so as to cause to crackle or until crackling stops; of salts</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081515"
	 b:glossaryEntry="undergo decrepitation"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081605">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to become, or to cause to become, covered with a network of small cracks; "The blazing sun crackled the desert sand"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081811"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make suburban in character; "highly suburbanized cities"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200081944"
	 b:glossaryEntry='take on suburban character; "the city suburbanized"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200082064">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[make or become different in some particular way, without permanently losing one''s or its former characteristics or essence; "her mood changes in accordance with the weather"; "Prices vary according to the season"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200082603">
	<b:glossaryEntry>vary the frequency, amplitude, phase, or other characteristic of (electromagnetic waves)</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200082765">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to modify microorganisms by repeated culture in the developing chick embryo</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200082918">
	<b:glossaryEntry>go or proceed from one point to another; "the debate moved from family values to the economy"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200083117">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(computer science) move through text or graphics in order to display parts that do not fit on the screen; "Scroll down to see the entire text"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200083323">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become glassy; of eyes; "Her eyes glaze over when she is bored"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200083483">
	<b:glossaryEntry>change radically; "E-mail revolutionized communication in academe"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200083639">
	<b:glossaryEntry>pass into a condition gradually, become;"The weather turned nasty"; "She grew angry"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200083826">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[grow bald; lose hair on one''s head; "He is balding already"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200083947">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to change; make different; cause a transformation; "The advent of the automobile may have altered the growth pattern of the city"; "The discussion has changed my thinking about the issue"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200089996"
	 b:glossaryEntry="debase through carnal gratification"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090111">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bleach and alter the natural development of (a green plant) by excluding sunlight</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090266"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make barbarous"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090367"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make alkaline, as of chemical substances"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090483"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make into a myth; "mythologize stories or events"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090619"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make into an allegory; of stories"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090728">
	<b:glossaryEntry>remove the mythical element (from writings, such as the Bible)</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200090879"
	 b:glossaryEntry='bring into a different state; "this may land you in jail"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091066"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make secular, as of societies; "Ataturk secularized Turkey"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091201"
	 b:glossaryEntry="coat or impregnate with rubber, as of fabrics"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091322"
	 b:glossaryEntry="coat a metal with an oxide coat"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091418"
	 b:glossaryEntry="cause to form a salt or ester of citric acid"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091527"
	 b:glossaryEntry="bring to a chemical stasis or equilibrium"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091645"
	 b:glossaryEntry='leave unchanged or unaltered; "leave it as is"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200091848"
	 b:glossaryEntry='have an effect upon; "Will the new rules affect me?"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200092182">
	<b:glossaryEntry>produce an affect or strain on somebody; "Each step told on his tired legs"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200092330">
	<b:glossaryEntry>have an affect for good or ill: "Her efforts will redound to the general good"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200092473"
	 b:glossaryEntry="subject to the action of bacteria"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200092585"
	 b:glossaryEntry='change to the contrary; "The trend was reversed"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200093046">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause a complete reversal of the circumstances; "The tables are turned now that the Republicans are in power!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200093237"
	 b:glossaryEntry="reverse the direction of an electric current"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200093348"
	 b:glossaryEntry="convert alternating to direct current"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200093452"
	 b:glossaryEntry="alter by alchemy, as of chemical elements"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200093560"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make alcoholic, as by fermenting"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200093668"
	 b:glossaryEntry="change in physical make_up"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200094296"
	 b:glossaryEntry="change over, change around, or switch over"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200094443"
	 b:glossaryEntry="assume a different shape or form"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200094820">
	<b:glossaryEntry>give individual shape or form to; "Language that individuates his memories"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200094964"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become granular"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200095054"
	 b:glossaryEntry='form a knot or bow in; "tie a necktie"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200095154">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make into terraces as for cultivation; "The Incas terraced their mountainous land"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200095301"
	 b:glossaryEntry='shape like a fork: "She forked her fingers"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200095406"
	 b:glossaryEntry="form a constellation or cluster"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200095506">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to shape or form; "shape a bun"; "shape a ball from the dough"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096156"
	 b:glossaryEntry="shape or form to required dimensions"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096259"
	 b:glossaryEntry='shape by rolling; "roll a cigarette"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096357">
	<b:glossaryEntry>flatten, stretch, or mold metal or glass, by rolling or by pulling it through a die or by stretching; "draw steel"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096541">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause (an arc) to form (as between electrodes of an arc lamp)</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096666">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to take on a definite and clear shape; "He tried to crystallize his thoughts"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096818"
	 b:glossaryEntry='form into twists; "Twist the bacon around the sausage"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200096935">
	<b:glossaryEntry>rise to, or form, a summit; "The helmet culminated in a crest"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097065"
	 b:glossaryEntry="form into grains"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097174"
	 b:glossaryEntry="form into slivers, as of wool"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097267"
	 b:glossaryEntry="form into a ridge"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097347">
	<b:glossaryEntry>form a plume: "The chimneys were pluming the sky"; "The engine was pluming black smoke"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097497"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become globular"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097591"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make round"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097706"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make cone-shaped"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097792"
	 b:glossaryEntry="shape or cut in scallops, as of the edge of a garment"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200097920">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make square; "Square the circle"; "square the wood with a file"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200098059"
	 b:glossaryEntry='express as a round number; "round off the amount"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200098208">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[contract one''s lips; "She primmed her lips after every bite of food"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200098338"
	 b:glossaryEntry="contract one''s lips into a rounded shape"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200098459"
	 b:glossaryEntry="round one''s lips as if intending to kiss"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200098574">
	<b:glossaryEntry>undergo a transformation or a change of position; "We turned from Socialism to Capitalism"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200100153">
	<b:glossaryEntry>pass suddenly and passively into a state of body or mind; "fall into a trap"; "She fell ill"; "They fell out of favor"; "Fall in love"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200100649"
	 b:glossaryEntry="diminish in size or intensity"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200100756">
	<b:glossaryEntry>begin to experience feelings of love towards; "She fell in love with her former student"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200100922">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to be held in suspension in a fluid, of particles, in chemistry</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200101074"
	 b:glossaryEntry="put back into suspension, as of particles, in chemistry"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200101196">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become sober after excessive alcohol consumption; "Keep him in bed until he sobers up"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200101375">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become more realistic; "After thinking about the potential consequences of his plan, he sobered up"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200101548"
	 b:glossaryEntry='cause to become sober; "A sobering thought"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200101662">
	<b:glossaryEntry>enter or assume a certain state or condition; "He became annoyed when he heard the bad news"; "It must be getting more serious"; "her face went red with anger"; "She went into ecstasy"; "Get going!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200102193">
	<b:glossaryEntry>adapt or conform oneself; "We must adjust to the bad economic situation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200102489">
	<b:glossaryEntry>behave in accordance or in agreement with; "Follow a pattern"; "Follow my example"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200102690">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[be or act in accordance with; "Go by this rule and you''ll be safe"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200102827">
	<b:glossaryEntry>adjust anew; "After moving back to America, he had to readjust"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200102974"
	 b:glossaryEntry="adjust in size relative to other things"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200103125"
	 b:glossaryEntry="cause somebody to adapt or reform socially or politically"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200103251"
	 b:glossaryEntry='adapt anew; "He readapted himself"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200103366">
	<b:glossaryEntry>decrease in size, extent, or range; "The amount of homework decreased towards the end of the semester"; "The cabin pressure fell dramatically"; "her weight fall to under a hundred pounds"; "his voice fell to a whisper"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200104055">
	<b:glossaryEntry>decrease in size, range, or extent; ""His earnings shrank"; "My courage shrivelled when I saw the task before me"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200104242"
	 b:glossaryEntry='diminish gradually; "Interested tapered off"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200104349">
	<b:glossaryEntry>fall or diminish; "The number of students in this course dropped off after the first test"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200104505"
	 b:glossaryEntry="decrease rapidly, as of money"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200104604"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make bigger or more; "The boss finally increased her salary"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200105152">
	<b:glossaryEntry>increase in quantity or bulk by adding a cheaper substance; "stretch the soup by addding some more cream"; "extend the casserole with a little rice"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200105400">
	<b:glossaryEntry>enlarge or increase; "The recent speech of the PLO chairman augmented tensions in the Near East"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200105569"
	 b:glossaryEntry='enlarge or increase; "build up excitement"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200105685"
	 b:glossaryEntry="increase at a rapidly accelerating rate"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200105798"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make larger; "She enlarged the flower beds'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200105931"
	 b:glossaryEntry='raise; "up the ante"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106011"
	 b:glossaryEntry='fall sharply; "stock prices broke"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106108"
	 b:glossaryEntry="increase in value; as of prices or numbers"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106300">
	<b:glossaryEntry>go or move upward; "The stock market soared after the cease-fire was announced"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106442">
	<b:glossaryEntry>rise in rank or status; "Her new novel jumped high on the bestseller list"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106604">
	<b:glossaryEntry>increase suddenly and significantly; "Prices jumped overnight"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106728"
	 b:glossaryEntry='grow by addition, as of capital: "The interest accrues"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106865"
	 b:glossaryEntry='be added; "Everything he does redounds to himself"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200106980"
	 b:glossaryEntry="advance in price, as of stocks"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200107072">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make less strong or severe; "he eased off the gas pedal and the car slowed down"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200107243"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become less intense"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200107371">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become bigger or greater in amount; "The amount of work increased"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200107863"
	 b:glossaryEntry='have an increased effect; "This adds to my worries"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200107978"
	 b:glossaryEntry='increase in; "gain momentum"; "gain nerve"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108091">
	<b:glossaryEntry>increase rapidly and in an uncontrolled manner; "The population of India is exploding"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108242"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become larger or bigger"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108348"
	 b:glossaryEntry='grow or intensify; "The pressure augmented"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108456">
	<b:glossaryEntry>grow or intensify; "Pressure is building up at the Indian-Pakistani border"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108597">
	<b:glossaryEntry>increase rapidly and progressively step by step on a broad base</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108725">
	<b:glossaryEntry>rise in rate or price; "The stock market gained 24 points today"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108869"
	 b:glossaryEntry="increase or accumulate at a rapidly accelerating rate"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200108988">
	<b:glossaryEntry>raise the level or amount of something; "raise my salary"; "raise the price of bread"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109154"
	 b:glossaryEntry="increase or raise, as of prices"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109250"
	 b:glossaryEntry='collect or gather; "Journals are accumulating in my office"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109474"
	 b:glossaryEntry="accumulate and create a backlog"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109570">
	<b:glossaryEntry>grow or become attached by accretion; "The story accreted emotion"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109701"
	 b:glossaryEntry="as of debts or scores"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109786">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[become similar to one''s environment; "Immigrants often want to assimilate quickly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200109988"
	 b:glossaryEntry="assimilate culturally"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110104"
	 b:glossaryEntry="cause members of a tribe to lose their cultural identity"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110229"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make similar"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110327"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become similar in sound; in phonetics"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110458"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become dissimilar"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110580"
	 b:glossaryEntry="make dissimilar"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110682">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become dissimilar by changing the sound qualities; of phonetics; "These consonants dissimilate"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200110872">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make undone; revert to the original condition or situation; "You cannot undo the damage!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200111031">
	<b:glossaryEntry>exchange or replace with another, usually of the same kind or category; "Could you convert my dollars into pounds?" "He changed his name"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200111343"
	 b:glossaryEntry="exchange a penalty for a less severe one"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200111469"
	 b:glossaryEntry="convert into capital, as of a company''s reserve funds"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200111608">
	<b:glossaryEntry>capitalize beyond what the business or the profit-making prospects warrant</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200111754"
	 b:glossaryEntry="cause transduction; as of energy forms"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200111859">
	<b:glossaryEntry>substitute a person or thing for (another that has ceased to fulfil its function); "He replaced the old razor blade"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200112100">
	<b:glossaryEntry>remove or replace the coverings of; "Father had to learn how to change the baby"; "After each guest we changed the bed linens"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
