</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200238678"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become immaterial; disappear"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200238795">
	<b:glossaryEntry>happen, occur, or be the case in the course of events or by chance; "It happens that today is my birthday"; "These things befell" (Santayana)</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239038"
	 b:glossaryEntry='happen as a result; "Nothing good will come of this"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239152">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become of; happen to; "He promised that no harm would befall her"; "What has become of my children?"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239336"
	 b:glossaryEntry="produce as a consequence or an unplanned result"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239449"
	 b:glossaryEntry='happen simultaneously; "The two events coincided"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239591"
	 b:glossaryEntry='concur partially or wholly; "Our vacations overlap"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239707">
	<b:glossaryEntry>start abruptly; "After 1989, peace broke out in the former East Bloc"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239851"
	 b:glossaryEntry='start to grow or develop; "a budding friendship"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200239960">
	<b:glossaryEntry>take the first step or steps in carrying out an action: "We began working at dawn"; "Who will start?" "Get working as soon as the sun rises!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200240453"
	 b:glossaryEntry='begin vigorously; "The prisoners fell to work right away"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200240572">
	<b:glossaryEntry>begin suddenly and sometimes violently; "He broke out shouting"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200240718"
	 b:glossaryEntry='take off or begin; "launch into a speech"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200240823">
	<b:glossaryEntry>set off quickly, usually with success; "The freshman set off to a good start in his math class"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200240992">
	<b:glossaryEntry>arrive at the point of; "She gets to fretting if I stay away form home too long"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200241136">
	<b:glossaryEntry>commence in a manner calculated to bring food luck: "They auspicated the trip with a bottle of champagne"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200241308">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[set to work upon; turn one''s energies vigorously to a task; "I attacked the problem as soon as I got out of bed"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200241484"
	 b:glossaryEntry="start in a certain activity, enterprise, or role"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200241598">
	<b:glossaryEntry>begin with vigor; "He launched into a long diatribe"; "She plunged into a dangerous adventure"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200241765">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become available; "water or electricity came on again after the earthquake"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200241905">
	<b:glossaryEntry>set out on (an enterprise, subject of study, etc.); "she embarked upon a new career"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200242079"
	 b:glossaryEntry='pursue or resume; "take up a matter for consideration"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200242198"
	 b:glossaryEntry='start to be active; "Get cracking, please!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200242403">
	<b:glossaryEntry>set in motion, cause to start; "The U.S. started a war in the Middle East"; "The Iraquis began hostilities"; "begin a new chapter in your life"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200242702">
	<b:glossaryEntry>be a precursor of; "The fall of the Berlin Wall ushered in the post-Cold War period"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200242877">
	<b:glossaryEntry>set in motion or cause to begin; "The guide set the tour off to a good start"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200243043"
	 b:glossaryEntry="persist from one stage or sphere of activity to another"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200243167"
	 b:glossaryEntry='take up or begin anew; "We resumed the negotiations"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200243335">
	<b:glossaryEntry>return to a previous location or condition: "The painting resumed its old condition when we restored it"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200243513">
	<b:glossaryEntry>be persistent, refuse to stop; "he persisted to call me every night"; "The child persisted and kept asking questions"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200243815">
	<b:glossaryEntry>persist with actions or an attitude despite the probability that it will cause trouble; "He is asking for trouble with his behavior"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200244033">
	<b:glossaryEntry>persist in working hard; "Students must plug away at this problem"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200244173"
	 b:glossaryEntry='keep to: "Stick to your principles"; "stick to the diet"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200244343">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bring to a conclusion or cause to come to an end; "We terminated our relation with the company"; "It is unclear whether the bombing of Hiroshima ended the war"; "Cease doing what you are doing!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200244698"
	 b:glossaryEntry='stop or cease; "leave off where you started"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200244809"
	 b:glossaryEntry='cause to stop or halt; "Halt the engine"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200244935">
	<b:glossaryEntry>go out of existence; "She hoped that the problem would eventually pass away"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245079"
	 b:glossaryEntry='terminate; "We closed out our account"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245184"
	 b:glossaryEntry='end, at least for a long time; "The correspondence lapsed"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245305">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to finish a relationship with somebody; "That finished me with Mary"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245443">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cease operating; as of machinery: "The pump suddenly cut out"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245569">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become extinguished; as of lights or candles; "The lights suddenly went out and we were in the dark"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245734">
	<b:glossaryEntry>be in a certain state as a result of some action or event; "He wound up being unemployed and living at home again"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200245987">
	<b:glossaryEntry>finally be or do something, as in "He ended up marrying his high school sweetheart"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200246153"
	 b:glossaryEntry='cease slowly; "Old habit die hard"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200246253">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bring to an end; "She ended their friendship when she found out that he had once been convicted of a crime"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200246783">
	<b:glossaryEntry>terminate before completion, as of a computer process, a mission, etc.</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200246916">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bring to a head or to the highest point; "Seurat culminated pointillism"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200247063">
	<b:glossaryEntry>put an end to, as of a siege or a blockade; "lift a ban"; "raise a siege"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200247214">
	<b:glossaryEntry>terminate, as of a project or a program; "The NSF axed the research program and stopped funding it"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200247379">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as of the flow of a liquid flowing, such as blood from a wound</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200247537">
	<b:glossaryEntry>arrest the motion (of something) abruptly; "He checked the flow of water by shutting off the main valve"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200247730">
	<b:glossaryEntry>disappear or come to an end; "Their anger died"; "My secret will die with me!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200247869"
	 b:glossaryEntry='end or extinguish by forceful means; "Stamp out poverty!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200248008">
	<b:glossaryEntry>destroy a vitally essential quality of or in; "Eating artichokes kills the taste of all other foods"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200248196"
	 b:glossaryEntry='cause to cease operating; "kill the engine"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200248337">
	<b:glossaryEntry>tire out completely; "The daily stress of her work is killing her"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200248483"
	 b:glossaryEntry='snap close with a sound; "The lock snapped shut"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200248593"
	 b:glossaryEntry='terminate (legally); "Their marriage dissolved"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200248733"
	 b:glossaryEntry="undergo or cause to undergo a change in the surface"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200249124"
	 b:glossaryEntry='become level or even; "The ground levelled off"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200249246">
	<b:glossaryEntry>form a crust or form into a crust; "The bread crusted in the oven"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200249393">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bend out of shape, as under pressure or from heat; "The highway buckled during the heatwave"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200249582">
	<b:glossaryEntry>rise upward, as from pressure or moisture; "The floor is lifting slowly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200249716"
	 b:glossaryEntry="produce buds, branches, or germinate; of plants"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200249893">
	<b:glossaryEntry>grow and flourish; "The burgeoning administration"; "The burgeoning population"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200250037"
	 b:glossaryEntry='develop buds, of plants; "The hibiscus is budding!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200250149"
	 b:glossaryEntry="take root; begin to grow; of plants"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200250254">
	<b:glossaryEntry>pass from physical life and lose all all bodily attributes and functions necessary to sustain life; "She died from cancer"; "They children perished in the fire"; "The patient went peacefully"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200250810"
	 b:glossaryEntry="be killed or die; (slang)"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200250909">
	<b:glossaryEntry>be abolished or discarded; "These ugly billboards have to go!" "These luxuries all had to go under the Khmer Rouge"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251084">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[be survived by after one''s death: "He left six children"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251236">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to be without a spouse; "The war widowed many women in the former Yugoslavia"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251382"
	 b:glossaryEntry='die by drowning in water; "The child drowned in the lake"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251502"
	 b:glossaryEntry='die (colloquial); "The old man finally kicked the bucket"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251737">
	<b:glossaryEntry>be born, used chiefly of lambs: "The lambs fell in the afternoon"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251864"
	 b:glossaryEntry='die before; die earlier than; "She predeceased her husband"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200251991"
	 b:glossaryEntry='come into existence through birth; "She was born on a farm"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200252195">
	<b:glossaryEntry>be born or come into existence; "All these flowers come to life when the rains come"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200252375"
	 b:glossaryEntry='become overcast; "the sky clouded over"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200252482"
	 b:glossaryEntry='become covered with mist; "The windshield misted over"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200252610"
	 b:glossaryEntry='free from mist; "demist the car windows"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200252740">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[become bloated or swollen or puff up; "The dead man''s stomach was bloated"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200252877">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[make bloated or swollen; "Hunger bloated the child''s belly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200253017">
	<b:glossaryEntry>form a curl, curve, or kink; "the cigar smoke curled up at the ceiling"; "The road curved"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200253202"
	 b:glossaryEntry='prevent completion; "stop the project"; "break the silence"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200253437">
	<b:glossaryEntry>stop and wait, as if awaiting further instructions or developments; "Hold on a moment!"; "We broke at noon"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200253624">
	<b:glossaryEntry>interrupt before its natural or planned end; "We had to cut short our vacation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200253822"
	 b:glossaryEntry="interrupt a telephone conversation"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200253929"
	 b:glossaryEntry='stop pursuing or acting; "drop a lawsuit"; "knock it off!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200254087">
	<b:glossaryEntry>drop persecution of by entering a nolle prosequi in the court records; "They nolle prossed the charge"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200254265">
	<b:glossaryEntry>stop a process or a habit by imposing a freeze on it; "Suspend the aid to the war-torn country"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200254442">
	<b:glossaryEntry>get stuck while doing something; "She bogged down many times while she wrote her dissertation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200254616">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to slow down or get stuck; "The vote would bog down the house"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200254764">
	<b:glossaryEntry>end prematurely; "She interrupted her pregnancy"; "break a lucky streak"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200254973"
	 b:glossaryEntry='close at the end of a session; "The court adjourned"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200255118">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[interrupt periodically; "Her sharp questions punctuated the speaker''s drone"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200255269">
	<b:glossaryEntry>heat food in order to kill harmful microorganisms; "pasteurize milk"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200255423">
	<b:glossaryEntry>undergo condensation; change from a gaseous to a liquid state; "water condenses"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200255605">
	<b:glossaryEntry>compress or concentrate; "Congress condensed the three-year plan into a six-month plan"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200255809">
	<b:glossaryEntry>develop due to condensation; "All our planets condensed out of the same material"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200255974">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become more compact or concentrated; "Her feelings condensed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200256119"
	 b:glossaryEntry="vaporize and then condense right back again"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200256293">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause a gas or vapor to change into a liquid; "The hot air condensed the steam"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200256456"
	 b:glossaryEntry='remove water from; "condense the milk"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200256596"
	 b:glossaryEntry="sublime once again, as of chemical compounds"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200256707">
	<b:glossaryEntry>lose or cause to lose liquid by vaporization leaving a more concentrated residue;"evaporate milk"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200256916"
	 b:glossaryEntry="exude water vapor; of plants"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257011">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become one; "Germany unified officially in 1990"; "Will the two Koreas unify?"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257266"
	 b:glossaryEntry='coalesce or unite in a mass; "Blood clots"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257385"
	 b:glossaryEntry="unite (beliefs or conflicting principles)"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257494">
	<b:glossaryEntry>break up or separate; "The country is disunifying"; "Yugoslavia broke apart after 1989"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257679">
	<b:glossaryEntry>come together so as to form a single product; "Social forces converged to bring the Fascists back to power"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257860"
	 b:glossaryEntry="unite to form a league"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200257954"
	 b:glossaryEntry="unite in a federation; of countries or nations"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258079"
	 b:glossaryEntry='turn into carbon, as by burning; "carbonize coal"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258213">
	<b:glossaryEntry>loose heat; The air cooled considerably after the thunderstorm"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258384"
	 b:glossaryEntry='lose intensity; "His enthusiasm cooled considerably"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258521">
	<b:glossaryEntry>get excessively and undesirably hot; "The car engines overheated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258652"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make cool or cooler; "Chill the food"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258851"
	 b:glossaryEntry='put ice on or put on ice; "Ice your sprained limbs"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200258963"
	 b:glossaryEntry='keep cool in a refrigerator; "refrigerate this medicine"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200259088"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make hot or hotter; "heat the soup"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200259391"
	 b:glossaryEntry="heat a metal prior to working it"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200259485">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in chemistry; heat a substance so that it oxidizes or reduces</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200259611"
	 b:glossaryEntry='heat beforehand; "Preheat the oven!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200259713">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make excessively or undesirably hot; "The room was overheated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200259859"
	 b:glossaryEntry='gain heat or get hot; "The room heated up quickly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260044"
	 b:glossaryEntry='make warm or warmer; "The blanket will warm you"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260180">
	<b:glossaryEntry>become more friendly or open; "She warmed up after we had lunch together"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260318"
	 b:glossaryEntry='get warm or warmer; "The soup warmed slowly on the stove"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260447"
	 b:glossaryEntry="warm by rubbing, as with the hands"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260552"
	 b:glossaryEntry='unite with carbon; "carburize metal"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260683">
	<b:glossaryEntry>burn or sear (tissue) using a hot iron or electric current or a caustic agent; "The surgeon cauterized the wart"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200260887"
	 b:glossaryEntry='change to ice; "The water in the bowl froze"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261073"
	 b:glossaryEntry="become frozen and covered with glaciers"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261178"
	 b:glossaryEntry="form into a solid mass; coalesce"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261276">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bring to, or maintain at, the boiling point, as of water and other liquids; "boil this liquid until it evaporates"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261496"
	 b:glossaryEntry="extract the essence of something by boiling it"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261606">
	<b:glossaryEntry>come to the boiling point and change from a liquid to vapor; "Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261817">
	<b:glossaryEntry>overflow or cause to overflow while boiling; "The milk is boiling over"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200261966">
	<b:glossaryEntry>store in a deepfreeze, as for conservation; "deep-freeeze the food"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200262110">
	<b:glossaryEntry>freeze rapidly so as to preserve the natural juices and flavors; "quick-freeze the shrimp"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200262285"
	 b:glossaryEntry='cause to freeze; "Freeze the leftover food"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200262454">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to thaw and become soft or liquid again; "The sub melted the ice"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200262648">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make or become free of frost or ice; "Defrost the car window"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200262798"
	 b:glossaryEntry='undergo combustion; "Maple wood burns well"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200263003">
