<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200281344">
	<b:glossaryEntry>coordinate in such a way that all parts work together effectively</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200281483">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make central; "The Russian government centralized the distribution of food"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200281684">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make less central; "After the revolution, food distribution was decentralized"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;200281907">
	<b:glossaryEntry>make socialist, as of governments or institutions; "Health care should be socialized!"</b:glossaryEntry>
