<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;201582922">
	<b:glossaryEntry>give over; surrender or relinquish to the physical control of another</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;201583087">
	<b:glossaryEntry>cause to have, in the abstract sense or physical sense: "She gave him a black eye"; "The draft gave me a cold"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;201583295">
	<b:glossaryEntry>bestow, esp. officially; "grant a degree"; "give a divorce"; "This bill grants us new rights"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;201583448">
	<b:glossaryEntry>pay with a credit card; pay with plastic money; postpone payment by recording a purchase as a debt; "Will you pay cash or charge the purchase?"</b:glossaryEntry>
