<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400311741">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an obedient manner; "obediently she slipped off her right shoe and stocking"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400311926">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a disobedient manner; "he went ahead disobediently and did what his superviser had warned him not to do"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400312111">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an impartially dispassionate manner; "although he was looking at the other girl, he did so dispassionately"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400312283">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a disparaging manner; "these mythological figures are described disparagingly as belonging `only to a story''"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400312487">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a dispirited manner without hope; "the first Mozartian opera to be subjected to this curious treatment ran dispiritedly for five performances"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400312722">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a displeasing manner; "he made displeasingly cutting remarks about his friends"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400312864">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a disproportionate degree; "his benefits were disproportionately generous"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313024">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a proportionate degree; "your salary will rise proportionately to your workload"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313222">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a disproportionate degree; "this wall is disproportionately long"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313373">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a proportionate degree; "the height of this wall must be reduced proportionately to give the room pleasant dimensions"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313574"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a disputatious manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313695">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a disquieting manner; "the disquietingly close sounds of gunfire"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313823"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a disreputable manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400313924"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a reputable manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314019">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a respectful manner; "might I respectfully suggest to the Town Council that they should adopt a policy of masterly inactivity?"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314245">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a disrespectful manner; "he treats his parents rather disrespectfully"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314398">
	<b:glossaryEntry>from or at a distance; "dimly, distantly, voices sounded in the stillness"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314528">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an offensively distasteful manner; "a distastefully explicit report on the Royal couple''s marital life"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314694">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[with distress; "`Doctor Rother says it''s his only chance,'' she added distressfully"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314819">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a distributive manner; "marine vertebrates have their weight supperted distributively by the water"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400314982">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as individuals or as separate units (not collectively); "taken distributively, their rights are imperceptible"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400315153"
	 b:glossaryEntry='with distrust; "she looked at him distrustfully"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400315313">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with trust; in a trusting manner; "she looked at her father trustingly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400315522">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a disturbing manner; "the details of the kidnaper''s letter had sounded disturbingly convincing"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400315679"
	 b:glossaryEntry="as a matter of doctrine"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400315760">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a narrow-minded dogmatic manner; "he is a dogmatically opinionated critic of Modern Art"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400315910">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with sadness; in a sorrowful manner; "his mother looked at him dolefully when he told her he had joined the Army"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316111">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with respect to home or family; "the housewife bored us with her domestically limited conversation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316269">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with respect to the internal affairs of a government; "domestically, the president proposes a more moderate economic policy"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316452"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a domineering manner; "his wife behaved domineeringly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316569"
	 b:glossaryEntry='two together; "some people sleep better double"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316651"
	 b:glossaryEntry='downward and forward; "he was bent double with pain"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316738">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[at a faster speed; "now let''s play the piece again double-quick"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400316857"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a doubtful manner; "Gerald shook his head doubtfully"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317000"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a dowdy unfashionable manner; "she dresses dowdily"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317168">
	<b:glossaryEntry>toward the bottom of a hill; "running downhill, he gained a lot of speed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317278">
	<b:glossaryEntry>toward a lower or inferior state; "your performance has been going downhill for a long time now"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317411"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a drab manner; "she dresses drably"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317502">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a dreamy manner; "`She would look beautiful in the new dress,'' Tommy said dreamily"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317684">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[with dry humor; "`Never mind the hole in the ceiling,'' he saiid drily"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317806"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a drooping manner; "a branch hung low, droopingly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400317916">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a drowsy manner; "`Time to get up,'' she said drowsily"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318060">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an inarticulate manner; "I nodded dumbly and he slit the envelope"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318182">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a stupid manner; "he had so rapaciously desired and so obtusely expected to find her alone"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318386">
	<b:glossaryEntry>out of a sense of duty; in a dutiful manner; "he dutifully visited his mother every Sunday"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318533">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a forceful dynamic manner; "this pianist plays dynamically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318653">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to, toward, or in the east; "we travelled east for several miles"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318751"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to, toward, or in the west; "we moved west to Arizona"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318838">
	<b:glossaryEntry>toward the west; "they traveled westward toward the setting sun"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400318951"
	 b:glossaryEntry='toward the east; "they migrated eastward to Sweden"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319051"
	 b:glossaryEntry='from the east; "the winds blew easterly all night"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319174"
	 b:glossaryEntry='from the west; "the wind blew westerly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319286">
	<b:glossaryEntry>toward the west; "we began to steer away westerly"- Daniel Defoe</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319405">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ebullient manner; "Khrushchev ebulliently promised to supply rockets for the protection of Cuba against American aggression"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319657">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ecclesiastic manner; "the candidate was ecclesiastically endorsed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319792">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with respect to ecology; "ecologically speaking, this idea is brilliant; economically, it is a disaster"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400319955">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ecstatic manner; "he reacted ecstatically to my plan to travel to Africa"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400320159">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with the edge forward or on, by, or toward the edge; "he sawed the board edgeways"; "held it edgewise"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400320309">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as if by an edge; barely; "I could not get a word in edgewise"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400320419">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an educational manner; "the assistant masters formed a committee of their own to consider what could be done educationally for the town"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400320618">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unnatural eery manner; "it was eerily quiet in the chapel"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400320764">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an effectual manner; "Bismarck was constantly criticised by the more liberal newspapers, and he retaliated by passing an emergency decree that effectually muzzled the press"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321016">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ineffectual manner; "she tried ineffectually to light the primus, and Thomas came to help her"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321194">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an effective manner; "these are real problems that can be dealt with most effectively by rational discussion"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321434">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ineffective manner; "he dealt with the problem rather ineffectively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321641"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an elementary manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321723"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an effusive manner; "the critics praised her effusively"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321839"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a demonstrative manner; "he greeted her demonstratively"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400321960"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an egotistical manner; "he behaved egotistically"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400322120">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unselfish manner; "he acted unselfishly when he helped her get the promotion"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400322279">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a gracefully elegant manner; "the members of these groups do not express themselves as accurately or as elegantly as their critics do"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400322472">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with elegance; in a tastefully elegant manner; "the room was elegantly decorated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400322627"
	 b:glossaryEntry="without elegance"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400322719"
	 b:glossaryEntry='with eloquence; "he expressed his ideas eloquently"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400322896">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without eloquence; in an inarticulate manner; "the freshman expresses his thoughts unarticulately"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323106">
	<b:glossaryEntry>causing embarrassment; "the great man was embarrassingly humble and self-effacing"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323249">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an eminent manner; "two subjects on which he was eminently qualified to make an original contribution"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323410">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a competitively imitative manner; "she emulously tried to outdo her older sister"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323550">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an encouraging manner; "`Go on,'' he said encouragingly to his student"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323701">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a discouraging manner; "the failure rate on the bar exam is discouragingly high"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323863">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with the end forward or toward the observer; "houses built endways"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400323985">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in or toward the direction of the ends; lengthwise; "endways pressure"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324101"
	 b:glossaryEntry='on end or upright; "sticks leaning against the wall endways"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324207">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an enterprising manner; "`Let''s go up that mountain,'' she said enterprisingly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324349">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an entertaining manner; "Byron''s consumed memoirs possessed the merit of being well and entertainingly written"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324524">
	<b:glossaryEntry>for the environment; "the new recycling policy is environmentally safe"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324657"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an equable manner; "he is an equably cheerful fellow"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324767">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an equitable manner; "the inheritance was equitably divided among the sisters"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400324922">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an inequitable manner; "their father''s possessions were inequitably divided among the sons"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400325092">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a straight-backed manner; "the old man still walks erectly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400325226">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with erudition; in an erudite manner; "he talked eruditely about Indian mythology"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400325394">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ethical manner; from an ethical point of view; according to ethics; "he behaved ethically"; "this is ethically unacceptable"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400325598"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an unethical manner; "he behaved unethically"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400325722">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a euphemistic manner; "his violent death was euphemistically referred to as a passing away"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400325878">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with evasion; in an evasive manner; "her husband seemed to know many of the people who were named, but he replied evasively when asked who they were"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400326083"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a level and regular way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400326180"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a regular way without variation; "try to breathe evenly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400326313"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an uneven and irregular way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400326416">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an irregular manner; "the patient is breathing irregularly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400326536">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in equal amounts or shares; in a balanced or impartial way; "a class evenly divided between girls and boys"; "they split their winnings equally"; "deal equally with rich and poor"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400326832">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unequal or partial manner; "profits were distributed unevenly"; "angry at being dealt with so unequally"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400327063">
	<b:glossaryEntry>at any future time; in the future; "lead a blameless life evermore"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400327181">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an exciting manner; "at the time of its appearance, the movie must have seemed excitingly new, even revolutionary"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400327373">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unexciting manner; "this painting was nothing more but an unexcitingly grey canvas with a few red speckles"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400327563">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an excusable manner or to an excusable degree; "he was excusably late"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400327808">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unpardonable manner or to an unpardonable degree; "he was inexcusably cruel to his wife"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328080">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to an exorbitant degree; "prices are exorbitantly high in the capital"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328275"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an expedient manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328405"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an inexpedient manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328507">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an expensive manner; "an expensively dressed little man turned a corner and approached her"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328677">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a cheap manner; "a cheaply dressed woman approached him in the bar"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328863">
	<b:glossaryEntry>suddenly and rapidly; "the population in Central America is growing explosively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400328983">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an explosive manner; "the political situation in Kashmir and Jammu is explosively unstable"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400329135">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an exponential manner; "inflation is growing exponentially"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400329257"
	 b:glossaryEntry='by express; "please send the letter express"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400329337">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with expression; in an expressive manner; "she gave the order to the waiter, using her hands very expressively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400329507">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without expression; in an inexpressive manner; "she looked at him inexpressively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400329649"
	 b:glossaryEntry='without prior preparation; "he spoke extemporaneously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400329812">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a wasteful manner; "the United States, up to the 1920s, used fuel lavishly, mainly because it was so cheap"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400330011">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an exuberant manner; "the exuberantly baroque decoration of the church"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400330173"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a faddish manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400330276">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a disloyal and faithless manner; "he behaved treacherously"; "his wife played him false"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400330532">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an incorrect manner; "to credit Lister with the first formulation of the basic principle of stratigraphy would be to bestow credit falsely"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400330760">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an insincerely false manner; "a seduction on my part would land us with the necessity to rise, bathe and dress, chat falsely about this and that, and emerge into the rest of the evening as though nothing had happened"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331034">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an intimately familiar manner; "Sid, as he was familiarly known by his friends, was one of the most respected and devoted members of the socialist minority group"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331256"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a superlative manner; "we got on famously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331338">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a passionately fanatic manner; "he followed the teachings of his guru fanatically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331481">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a fanciful manner; "the Christmas tree was fancifully decorated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331619"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a farcical manner; "a farcically inept bungler"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331726">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a fashionable manner; "his voice had no trace of the drawl that you would expect to find in a fashionably dressed young man"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400331929">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unfashionable manner; "she seemed to make a point of being unfashionably dressed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400332094">
