</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400390758">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a maternal manner; as a mother; "she loved her students almost maternally"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400390903">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mawkish manner; "the violinist played that piece mawkishly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400391023">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a maximal degree; "the cells maximally responsive to lines in this orientation will fire"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400391189">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a minimal degree; "the cells minimally responsive to lines in this orientation will not fire"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400391359">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a meager degree or in a meager manner; "these voices are meagerly represented at the conference"; "the area is slenderly endowed with natural resources"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400391676">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to an ample degree or in an ample manner; "these voices were amply represented"; "we benefited richly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400391857">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a meandering manner; "the river ran meanderingly through the valley"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400391987">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a meaningful manner; so as to be meaningful; "He glanced at her meaningfully"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400392159">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a miserly manner; "they lived meanly and without ostentation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400392303"
	 b:glossaryEntry='poorly or in an inferior manner; "troops meanly equipped"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400392413">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a despicable, ignoble manner; "this new leader meanly threatens the deepest values of our society"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400392623">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to an immeasurable degree; beyond measurement; "the war left him immeasurably fearful of what man can do to man"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400392812"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to a measurable degree; "the difference is measurably large"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400392947">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mechanistic manner; "Handel achieves a huge breadth of musical thought when composing almost mechanistically in the least weighty of styles"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393136">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a medial position; "this consonant always occurs medially"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393252">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a meditative manner; "round and round, while meditatively, as a cow chewing the cud, he let his eyes rest on the flat water ahead of him"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393451"
	 b:glossaryEntry="(obsolete) in a mellow manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393544"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a melodious manner; "she sang melodiously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393695"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an unmelodious manner; "she sings rather unmelodiously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393831">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an overly emotional manner; "she acted melodramatically when she called for help"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400393978">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as in a melodrama; "here, the hero is melodramatically reunited with the heroine"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400394122">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a memorable manner; "Horowitz could play Chopin memorably"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400394291"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an unmemorable manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400394391">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a menacing manner; "the voice at the other end of the line dropped menacingly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400394563">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mendacious and untruthful manner; "I told him, quite untruthfully, that I had just returned from leave"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400394781">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with truth; "I told him truthfully that I had just returned from my vacation"; "he answered the question as truthfully as he could"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400394987"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a menial manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400395060">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without pity; in a merciless manner; "he was mercilessly trounced by his opponent in the House"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400395311">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a meretricious manner; "the boat is meretriciously decorated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400395465">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a meritorious manner; "he served his country meritoriously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400395587">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a messy, untidy manner; "Rossi spat very deliberately, and very messily, upon Durieux''s party card"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400395772">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tidy manner; "the door gave access to a tidily furnished sitting-room where chintz and oak predominated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400395934"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a methodical manner; "let us proceed methodologically"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396054"
	 b:glossaryEntry='with regard to meter; "metrically, these poems are matched"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396170">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a rhythmic manner; "the chair rocked rhythmically back and forth"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396297">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unreasonably senseless manner; "these temples were mindlessly destroyed by the Red Guards"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396482">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without intellectual involvement; "all day long, he mindlessly filled out forms"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396619">
	<b:glossaryEntry>at or near or toward the center of a ship; "in the late 19th century, engines were placed in front, amidships, and at the rear"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396806"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in the middle of the week"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396867">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mincing manner; "she stepped mincingly over the puddles"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400396984">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in the manner of a clergyman; "he was called on to visit ministerially on the dying man"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397132">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in minute detail; "our inability to see everything minutely and clearly is due merely to the infirmity of our senses"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397323">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a miraculous manner; "my hand grasped the gun that was, miraculously, lying on the ground beside my finger tips"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397497"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a miserable manner; "I bit my lip miserably and nodded"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397611">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a misty manner; "the summits of the mountains were mistily purple"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397734"
	 b:glossaryEntry='(in music) much; "allegro molto"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397800"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a momentous way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400397876">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a monotonous manner; "the history of the play throughout the latter part of the eighteenth century is monotonously uneventful"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400398064">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a moody manner; "in the bar, a youngish, sharp-eyed man was staring moodily into a gin and tonic"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400398218">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a morbid manner or to a morbid degree; "he was morbidly fascinated by dead bodies"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400398358"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a morose manner; "he fell morosely on the bed"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400398462">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a morphological manner; with regard to morphology; "these two words are morphologically related"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400398623">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in such a manner that death ensues (also in reference to hatred, jealousy, fear, etc.); "a being of whom the forest Indians are said to be mortally afraid, with a hoof shaped like the heel of a bottle"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400398861">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without moving; in a motionless manner; "he saw the black-haired man waiting motionlessly behind the opposite side of the platform"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399051">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[with sadness; in a sad manner; "`She died last night,'' he said sadly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399172">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mournful manner; "the young man stared into his glass mournfully"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399299">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mundane manner; "the young man spoke so mundanely of university life"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399429">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as if bent on murder; "the huge dog bore down on them with bared fangs and barking murderously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399582">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a murky manner; "I could see that murkily passionate gesture"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399700"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a musical manner; "She sang very musically"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399820"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an unmusical manner; "She sings rather unmusically"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400399950">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a reflective manner; "`It''s funny about that bar,'' he said musingly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400400076">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a mutual or shared manner; "the agreement was mutually satisfactory"; "the goals of the negotiators were not reciprocally exclusive"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400400299">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[(often followed by `for'') in exchange or in reciprocation; "gave up our seats on the plane and in return received several hundred dollars and seats on the next plane out"; "we get many benefits in return for our taxes"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400400588">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a naive manner; "he believed, naively, that she would leave him her money"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400400719">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without clothing; "Henriette saw the weaving figure of an Apache warrior reel nakedly on a pony and rush by with a rifle raised"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400400901">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an exposed manner; without protection or defense; "they were attacked as they huddled nakedly on the bare hill"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400401069">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a narrow-minded manner; "narrow-mindedly, the authorities closed down the cafe where teenagers used to hang out"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400401299">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a broad-minded manner; "the authorities broad-mindedly permitted the opening of a center for teenagers"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400401484">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a nasty ill-tempered manner; "`Don''t expect me to help you,'' he added nastily"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400401646">
	<b:glossaryEntry>extending throughout an entire nation; "nationally advertised"; "it was broadcast nationwide"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400401850">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a natty manner; with smartness; "it was arranged carefully and nattily"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400401978">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a jaunty fashionable manner; "his hat sat jauntily on his full brown hair"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400402110">
	<b:glossaryEntry>not this merely but also; not only so but; "each of us is peculiar, nay, in a sense unique"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400402233">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[(comparative of `near'' or `close'') within a shorter distance; "come closer, my dear!"; "they drew nearer"; "getting nearer to the true explanation"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400402433">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[(superlative of `near'' or `close'') within the shortest distance; "that was the time he came nearest to death"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400402598">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an essential manner; "such expenses are necessarily incurred"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400402768">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as a highly likely consequence; "we are necessarily bound for federalism in Europe"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400402891">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unnecessary manner; "dust kills; if we make dust unnecessarily, we are killers"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403054">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a nefarious manner or to a nefarious degree; "nefariously involved in a consiracy"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403197"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a neglectful manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403278"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a negligent manner; "he did his work negligently"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403388">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an anxiously nervous manner; "we watched the stock market nervously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403515">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a neurotic manner; "they are finely, not to say neurotically adjusted"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403647">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with nervous excitement; "our bodies jumped nervously away at the slightest touch"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403785"
	 b:glossaryEntry='at no time hereafter; "Quoth the raven, nevermore!" -E.A.Poe'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400403897">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[near in time or place or relationship; "as the wedding day drew near"; "stood near the door"; "don''t shoot until they come near"; "getting near to the true explanation"; "her mother is always near"; "The end draws nigh"; "the bullet didn''t come close"; "don''t get too close to the fire"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404231">
	<b:glossaryEntry>very close; "without my reading glasses I can hardly see things close up"; "even firing at close range he missed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404398"
	 b:glossaryEntry='at the end of each day; "she checks on her roses nightly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404505"
	 b:glossaryEntry='by a factor of nine; "my investment has increased ninefold"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404614"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a noble manner; "she has behaved nobly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404708"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in no manner; "We could nohow make out his handwriting"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404809">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without stopping; "we are flying nonstop form New York to Tokyo"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400404909">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a nostalgic manner; "they spent an hour together, talking nostalgically as they wandered slowly down the coast road"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405087">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a notorious degree; "European emigres, who notoriously used to repair to the British Museum to write seditious pamphlets"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405251">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with regard to nutrition; "nutritionally, her new diet is suicide"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405377">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in number; with regard to numbers; "in ten years'' time the Oxbridge mathematicians, scientists, and engineers will not be much more significant numerically than the Oxbridge medical schools are now"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405633"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a numb manner; without feeling; "I stared at him numbly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405776"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in no manner; "they are nowise different"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405867"
	 b:glossaryEntry="to, toward, or in the northeast"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400405948"
	 b:glossaryEntry="to, toward, or in the northwest"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406029"
	 b:glossaryEntry="to, toward, or in the north-northeast"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406127"
	 b:glossaryEntry="to, toward, or in the north-northwest"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406225"
	 b:glossaryEntry='with objectivity; "we must look at the facts objectively"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406358">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a subjective way; "you cannot look at these facts subjectively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406501"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to an obscene degree; "this man is obscenely rich"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406589">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an obsequious manner; "she acts obsequiously toward her boss"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406776"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an observant manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400406888">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in manner that attracts attention; "obstreperously, he demanded to get service"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407069"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an obtrusive manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407167">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unobtrusive manner; "messengers were moving unobtrusively over the jet-black mountain ranges, bearing confidential tidings from sheikhdom to sheikhdom"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407402">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an officious manner; "nothing so fatal as to strive too officiously for an abstract quality like beauty"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407567">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an obstructive manner; "he acted very obstructively when we tried to carry out our project"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407753"
	 b:glossaryEntry="illegally in advance of the ball or puck"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407829"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an onerous manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400407905">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an opaque manner; "he referred opaquely to her recent past"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408022">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in respect to operation; "reported the machine operationally satisfactory"; "a well-trained staff that is operationally adequate"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408211">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a heavy and oppressive way; "it was oppressively hot in the office"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408340"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an optimal and most desirable way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408432">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[with optimism; in an optimistic manner; "`We have a good chance of winning,'' he exclaimed optimistically"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408616">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with pessimism; in a pessimistic manner; "he evaluated his chances for survival rather pessimistically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408799"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an optional manner; "this rule is applied optionally"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400408930"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an obligatory manner; "this rule applies obligatorily"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409064">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a sumptuous and opulent manner; "this government building is sumptuously appointed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409238">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with regard to organization; "organizationally, the conference was a disaster!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409380"
	 b:glossaryEntry="by means of osmosis"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409457">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ostentatious manner; "Mr Khrushchev ostentatiously wooed and embraced Castro at the U.N. general assembly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409677">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an outlandish manner; "the Bavarian was outlandishly dressed in lederhosen "</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409815">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an outspoken manner; "he was outspokenly critical of the Government''s new social policy"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400409964"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an overbearing manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410048"
	 b:glossaryEntry='on or to the other side of a page; "data tabulated overleaf"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410145">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[more than necessary; "she eats too much"; "let''s not blame them overmuch"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410266"
	 b:glossaryEntry='beyond or across the sea; "He lived overseas for many years"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410373">
	<b:glossaryEntry>over the side of a boat; "Willie eased himself overside into the sea"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410479">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an owlish manner; "the gentle-looking barrister peered owlishly around him"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410612">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pacifistic manner; "the pacifistically inclined liberals"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410735">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a fastidious and painstaking manner; "it is almost a waste of time painstakingly to learn the routines of selling"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400410946"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a palatable way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411038">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unpalatable way; "The vegetables looked unpalatably wilted"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411179">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pale manner; without physical or emotional color; "his wife, always palely appealing"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411322">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a manner lacking interest or vitality; "a palely entertaining show"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411482">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as someone winded and out of breath; "he came running after us pantingly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411641"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a parental manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411718">
	<b:glossaryEntry>by parenteral means; "the drug is intended to be administered parenterally"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400411852">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a parenthetical manner; "he added parenthetically that he would not attend the wedding ceremony"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412013"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a parochial manner; "parochially narrow in his outlook"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412129"
	 b:glossaryEntry='so as to pass a given point; "every hour a train goes past"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412226"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in spots"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412289">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a paternal manner; "he behaves very paternally toward his young bride"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412419">
	<b:glossaryEntry>arousing scornful pity; "they had pathetically little money"; "it was pathetically bad"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412565">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a manner arousing sympathy and compassion; "the sick child cried pathetically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412734">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a patriotic manner; "patriotically, he buys only U.S.-made products"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400412883">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unpatriotic manner; "unpatriotically he contrived a way of avoiding military service"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400413054">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a peaceable manner; "the tenant paying the rent hereby reserved and performing the several covenants herein on his part contained shall peaceably hold and enjoy the demised premises"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400413327">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a pedantic manner; "these interpretations are called `schemas'' or, more pedantically, `schemata''"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400413486"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a peevish manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400413625">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pejorative manner; "I am not using the word pejoratively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400413746">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with ability to see into deeply; "the author treats his subject penetratingly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400413918"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a pensive manner; "pensively he stared at the painting"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414032"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a penurious manner; "they lived penuriously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414137"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a perceptive manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414218">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with regard to perception; "this task is perceptually very difficult"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414346"
	 b:glossaryEntry='(archaic) through chance, "To sleep, perchance to dream.."'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414454">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a perfidious manner; "he was playing perfidiously one side against the other"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414593">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a perky manner; "stuck perkily, like a bustle on a woman''s skirt"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414707">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a perpendicular manner; "this red line runs perpendicularly to the green line"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400414850">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a perplexed manner; "he looked at his professor perplexedly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415004">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a persistent manner; "he was asking questions, unavoidable questions, persistently..."</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415152">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a persuasive manner; "this essay argues so persuasively..."</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415273">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a dogged and pertinacious manner; "he struggled pertinaciously for the new resolution"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415423">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pertinent way; "what is singular about his use of them is that no other artist, of his time or any other, has painted them so directly, intimately and pertinently"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415649"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a pervasive manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415728"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a petty way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415796">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with regard to pharmacology; "pharmacologically, this plant could have important applications"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400415954">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a phenomenal degree; "his reaction was phenomenally quick"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416074"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a philanthropic manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416163">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a phlegmatic manner; "he accepted the decision phlegmatically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416289">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a picturesque manner; "in the building trade such a trader is picturesquely described as a `brass plate'' merchant"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416466">
	<b:glossaryEntry>a little bit at a time; "the research structure has developed piecemeal"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416620"
	 b:glossaryEntry='extremely and sharply; "it was bitterly cold"; "bitter cold"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416804"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a piggish manner; "piggishly, he took two pieces of cake"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400416920"
	 b:glossaryEntry='having a pinnate shape; "a pinnately compoud leaf"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417026"
	 b:glossaryEntry='(used of heat) extremely; "the casserole was piping hot"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417128">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with strong spices; in a spicy manner; "the soup was spicily flavored"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417282">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a placid and good-natured manner; "I put the questions, and she answered them placidly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417427">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a quiet and tranquil manner; "the sea now shimmered placidly before our eyes"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417562"
	 b:glossaryEntry="(music) with a light plucking staccato sound"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417644">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a direct and unequivocal manner; "I asked him point-blank whether he wanted the job"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417771">
	<b:glossaryEntry>after death; "these piano pieces were published posthumously"; "he was honored posthumously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400417922">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(music) extremely fast; as fast as possible; "this passage should be played prestissimo"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418050">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(music) slowing down; "this passage should be played rallentando"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418155"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to a recognizable degree; "he was recognizably slimmer now"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418291">
	<b:glossaryEntry>beyond recognition; in an unrecognizable manner; "he had unrecognizably aged"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418464">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with regret (used in polite formulas); "I must regretfully decline your kind invitation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418592">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a piratical manner; "the piratically published edition of his book"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418720"
	 b:glossaryEntry='describing a rhythmic beating; "his heart went pit-a-pat"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418857"
	 b:glossaryEntry='as of footsteps; "he came running pit-a-pat down the hall"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400418995"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a piteous manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419070">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pithy sententious manner; "she expressed herself pithily"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419218">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a pitiful degree; "wages were pitifully low, particularly the wages of women"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419354"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a placating manner; "Jenny smiled placatingly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419443">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a disagreeable manner; "it''s so plaguey cold!"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419566">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a plaintive manner; "the last note of the song rang out plaintively"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419695">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a playful manner; "she loosened the half-hoop of diamonds on her left hand third finger and held it out to him playfully"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419875"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a pleasing manner; "the room was pleasingly large"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400419985">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a plenary manner; "an empire destined to enter the Commonwealth plenarily"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420118"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a pliant manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420191">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a plodding manner; "this writer ploddingly accumulates detail after detail"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420326">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(informal) with a short hollow thud; "plop came the ball down to the corner of the green"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420456">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(informal) straight down especially heavily or abruptly; "the anchor fell plump into the sea"; "we dropped the rock plump into the water"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420627">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pneumatic manner; "at the present time the transmission is very often done hydraulically or pneumatically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420798">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a pointless manner; "he spent his life in pointlessly tiresome drudgery"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400420931"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a very malevolent manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421047">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a plucky manner; "he was Brentford''s defensive star in pluckily holding out the determined Reading raids for long periods"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421227"
	 b:glossaryEntry="conforming to the direction of a plumb line"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421304"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a heavy ponderous manner; "he moves ponderously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421413">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an uninterestingly ponderous manner; "the play was staged with ponderously realistic sets"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421564"
	 b:glossaryEntry='like a pop or with a pop; "everything went pop"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421643"
	 b:glossaryEntry="like the Pope; in a popish manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421731">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a portentous manner; "portentously, the engines began to roll"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421855">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a possessive manner; "he was sleeping, one arm flung possessively across his wife"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400421999">
	<b:glossaryEntry>having the postage paid by the sender; "I will send it post-paid"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400422114">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a manner having a powerful influence; "Clytemnestra''s ghost crying in the night for vengeance remained most potently in the audience''s mind"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400422344"
	 b:glossaryEntry="with a pout or in a pouting manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400422416">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a powerful manner; "the federal government replaced the powerfully pro-settler Sir Godfrey Huggins with the even tougher and more determined ex-trade unionist"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400422664"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a powerless manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400422743"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a practicable manner; so as to be feasible"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400422875">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a realistic manner; "we want to build a democratic society, but we must act pragmatically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423028">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a preeminent degree; "a wide variety of pre-eminently contemporary scenes"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423180">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a precarious manner; "being a precariously dominant minority is a difficult position for human nature to cope with"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423357">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(intensifier) extremely; "there is precious little time left"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423469"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a precious manner; "his preciously valuable collection"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423584">
	<b:glossaryEntry>abruptly; in a precipitous manner; "the mountains rose precipitously from the shore"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423728">
	<b:glossaryEntry>very suddenly and to a great degree; "conditions that precipitously increase the birthrate"; "prices rose sharply"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400423894"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a precocious manner; "her child behaves precociously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424009">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a predictable manner or to a predictable degree; "predictably, he did not like the news"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424158"
	 b:glossaryEntry='too soon; in a premature manner; "I spoke prematurely"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424299">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(of childbirth) before the end of the normal period of gestation; "the child was born prematurely"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424455">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with foresight; "more presciently than they superiors, these workers grasped the economic situation"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424641"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a carnal manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424714">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a presentable manner; "years ago in her white-painted infancy it must have hung presentably on the deck of some luxury liner"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424900"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a pressing manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400424977">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a presumptuous manner; "he presumptuously overstepped the doctor''s orders]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425114"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a pretentious manner; "this author writes pretentiously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425251">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unpretentious manner; "she was unpretentiously dressed even though she was the guest of honor"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425431"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a supernatural manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425553"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a pretty manner; "all this is most prettily done"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425660">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a priggish manner; "this professor acts so priggishly--like a moderator with a gavel!"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425806">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a prissy manner; "the new teacher alienates the children by behaving prissily"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400425969">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a primitive style or manner; "rather primitively operated foundries"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426098"
	 b:glossaryEntry="with reference to the origin or beginning"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426211">
	<b:glossaryEntry>by the use of probability theory; "we can calculate the position of the particles probabilistically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426375"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in such a way as to pose a problem"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426471">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a wasteful manner or to a wasteful degree; "we are still prodigally rich compared to others"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426654">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a prodigious degree; "the prices of farms rose prodigiously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426776">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an irreverent or profane manner; "he kept wondering profanely why everything bad happened to him"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400426932"
	 b:glossaryEntry='with curses; "muttering profanely"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427022">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a proficient manner; "he dealt proficiently with the problem"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427145"
	 b:glossaryEntry="without gain or profit"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427272"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to a prohibitive degree; "it is prohibitively expensive"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427388"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an indiscriminate manner; "she reads promiscuously"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427539">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an auspicious manner; "the afternoon had begun so promisingly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427662">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a matter-of-fact manner; "I applied my attention prosaically to my routine"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427816">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a prosy manner; "somewhat prosily and repetitively expounded"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400427934">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a protesting manner; "the bed creaked protestingly when the fat man sat down"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400428073">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in the manner of something that has become a byword; "this proverbially bitter plant, wormwood"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400428227">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a providential manner; as determined by providence; "his providentially destined role"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400428377">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a fortunately providential manner; "providentially the weather remained good"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400428518">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a provocative manner; "`Try it,'' he said provocatively"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400428668">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a prudish manner; "she acts prudishly, but I wonder whether she is really all that chaste"</b:glossaryEntry>
