	<b:glossaryEntry>(finance) without possessing something at the time it is contractually sold; "he made his fortune by selling short just before the crash"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400447339">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with a shudder; "shudderingly, she acknowledged to herself that she dared not face what lay before her"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400447483"
	 b:glossaryEntry='on or as if on a sidesaddle; "she rode sidesaddle"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400447572">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with a side facing an object; "the train hit the truck broadside"; "the wave caught the canoe broadside and capsized it"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400447730">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to toward or at one side; "darting eyes looking sidelong out of a wizened face"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400447869">
