</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400449036">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with a lack of courage and determination; "simperingly, the accused begged for mercy"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400449197"
	 b:glossaryEntry='without assistance; "I built this house single-handedly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400449313">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a singular manner or to a singular degree; "Lord T. was considered singularly licentious even for the courts of Russia and Portugal; he acquired three wives and fourteen children during his Portuguese embassy alone"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400449588">
