	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a sulky manner; "`What else could I do?'' said Graham sulkily"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465023">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without delay; in a summary manner; "the suspected spy was summarily executed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465157">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a superfluous manner; "superfluously, he added his silly comments to the discussion"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465304"
	 b:glossaryEntry="to a superlative degree"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465387">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a superstitious manner; "superstitiously he refused to travel on Friday the 13th"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465533">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an indifferently supine manner; "he called the tune to me and I supinely took it up"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465675">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with the face upward; "she was stretched supinely on her back"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465792">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a surreptitious manner; "he was watching her surreptitiously as she waited in the hotel lobby"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400465980">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to a surpassing degree; "she was a surpassingly beautiful woman"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400466103"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in the manner of one who is surprised"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400466198">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a sweeping manner; "he sweepingly condemned the entire population of the country for the war crimes"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400466358">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an affectionate or loving manner; "Susan Hayward plays the wife sharply and sweetly"; (`sweet'' is a poetic or informal variant for `sweetly'' as in "how sweet the moonlight sleeps upon this bank"- Shakespeare; "talking sweet to each other")]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400466662">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with great ease and success; "in spite of some mishaps, everything went swimmingly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400466795">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in synchrony; in a synchronous manner; "in four-chambered hearts, the two auricles move synchronously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400466957">
	<b:glossaryEntry>by synthesis; in a synthetic manner; "some of these drugs have been derived from opium and others have been produced synthetically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400467148">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tacit manner; by unexpressed agreement; "they are tactily expected to work 10 hours a day"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400467297">
	<b:glossaryEntry>showing tact or tactfulness; in a tactful manner; "he stepped tactfully in to prevent trouble"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400467465">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without tact; in a tactless manner; "at the moment of the murder, he is standing in front of television cameras and talking tactlessly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400467675">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[with regard to tactics; "the tactically useful province is still firmly in the rebels'' hands"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400467825">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tame manner; "the labour movement allowed itself to be run out of power tamely"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400467962"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a tangible manner; "virtue is tangibly rewarded"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468068">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a tart manner; "`Never mind your immortal soul,'' she said tartly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468189">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with taste; in a tasteful manner; "the house was tastefully decorated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468344">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without taste or in poor taste; in a tasteless manner; "the house was tastelessly decorated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468512"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a tasty manner; "the meal was tastily cooked"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468614">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a playfully teasing manner; "`You hate things to be out of order, don''t you?'' she said teasingly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468783"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a taut manner; "the rope was tautly stretched"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400468885">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with tears; in a tearful manner; "the man confessed tearfully to having beaten his wife"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469029">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a short and concise manner; "a particular bird, exactly and tersely described in the book of birds"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469221">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a telescopic manner; "each of the four legs contains a simple screw jack with a thrust bearing that is operated telescopically inside of two tubes"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469432">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a telling manner; "the plain manner of its style all the more tellingly points up the horror of the case"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469596">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without extravagance; "these preferences are temperately stated"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469718">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with restraint; "he used the privileges of his office temperately"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469824">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tendentious manner; "the paper reported rather tendentiously on the war atrocities"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400469972">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with tenderness; in a tender manner; "tenderly she placed her arms round him"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470104">
	<b:glossaryEntry>(in enumerating something, such as topics or points of discussion) in the tenth place</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470225">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an ill-natured and tetchy manner; "`Are you sure?'' he asked her tetchily"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470356">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a theological manner; "he dealt with the problem of evil theologically, not philosophically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470511">
	<b:glossaryEntry>as regards theology; "the candidate was found theologically sound"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470637">
	<b:glossaryEntry>by thermostat; in a thermostatic manner; "the temperature is thermostatically controlled"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470789">
	<b:glossaryEntry>by a factor of three; "our rent increased threefold in the past five years"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400470916">
	<b:glossaryEntry>according to tradition; in a traditional manner; "traditionally, we eat fried foods on Hanukah"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400471071"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in quick succession; "misfortunes come fast and thick"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400471169">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a widely distributed manner; "thinly overgrown mountainside"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400471303">
	<b:glossaryEntry>spoken with poor articulation as if with a thick tongue; "after a few drinks he was beginning to speak thickly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400471468">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with thickness; in a thick manner; "spread 1/4 lb softened margarine or cooking fat fairly thickly all over the surface"; "we were visiting a small, thickly walled and lovely town with straggling outskirt"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400471745">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a small quantity or extent; "spread the margarine thinly over the meat"; "apply paint lightly"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400471923"
	 b:glossaryEntry='without viscosity; "the blood was flowing thin"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472048"
	 b:glossaryEntry='without force or sincere effort; "smiled thinly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472149"
	 b:glossaryEntry='with a thick consistency; "the blood was flowing thick"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472284">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a thirsty manner; "we drank thirstily from the bottle that was passed around"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472420">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a thrifty manner; "a used towel that he had used and had left thriftily on the ledge below the mirror rather than consign to the linen basket"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472621">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a thriftless manner; "he lives thriftlessly from day to day"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472743">
	<b:glossaryEntry>from one end or side to the other; "jealousy pierced her through"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472844"
	 b:glossaryEntry='over the whole distance; "this bus goes through to New York"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400472940"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in diameter; "this cylinder measures 15 inches through"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473031"
	 b:glossaryEntry='from beginning to end; "read this book through"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473114"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to completion; "think this through very carefully!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473201"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a timorous and trepid manner"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473319"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to the highest extent; "the shoes fit me tip-top"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473404"
	 b:glossaryEntry='on tiptoe or as if on tiptoe; "standing tiptoe"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473486"
	 b:glossaryEntry="the next day, the day after, following the present day"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473577">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a monotone; "`Come in,'' she said tonelessly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473681">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with regard to topography; "the geological environment is the primary factor in determining the character of a country not only topographically but historically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400473904"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a tortuous manner; "tortuously haggling over the price"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474001"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a touchy manner; "he touchily refused all offers to help"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474116"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a ruggedly tough manner; "toughly vigorous story-telling"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474230"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a transcendental way or to a transcendental extent"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474346">
	<b:glossaryEntry>for a very short time; "these three pions may actually be joined together transiently as a compound particle during the interchange process"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474544"
	 b:glossaryEntry="as a transitional step or in a transitional manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474655"
	 b:glossaryEntry="for a very brief time"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474735">
	<b:glossaryEntry>so as to allow the passage of light; "the red brilliance of the claret shines transparently in our glasses"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400474902">
	<b:glossaryEntry>so as to be easily understood or seen through; "his transparently lucid prose"; "his transparently deceitful behavior"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475080">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tremulous manner; "the leaves rustled tremulously in the wind"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475205">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in a vigorous and effective manner; "he defended his client''s civil rights trenchantly"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475350"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a trite manner; "tritely expressed emotions"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475451">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a frivolously trivial manner; "trivially motivated requests"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475570">
	<b:glossaryEntry>with little effort; "we can prove trivially that this theorem is false"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475697">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tropical manner; "it was tropically hot in the greenhouse"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475817">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a defiantly truculent manner; "the boy looked up truculently at his teacher"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400475954">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an aggressively truculent manner; "they strive for security by truculently asserting their own interests"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476120">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a tumultuous and riotous manner; "the crowd was demonstrating tumultuously"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476287">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a turbulent manner; with turbulence; "the river rolls turbulently boiling"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476422">
	<b:glossaryEntry>by tutorials; in a tutorial manner; "undergraduates are better taught tutorially"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476560"
	 b:glossaryEntry='by a factor of two; "the price increased twofold last year"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476667"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in a typographic way"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476749"
	 b:glossaryEntry="beyond the scope or in excess of legal power or authority"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476846">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[in an unaccountable manner; "in the book, a tycoon unaccountably becomes the hero''s friend"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400476997">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unalterable and unchangeable manner; "his views were unchangeably fixed"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400477229">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unarguable and undisputed manner; "you write as if this fact whilst inarguably forever condemning me to the ranks of Bohemianism nevertheless earned for me the right of entry into any company"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400477517">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unassuming manner; "she is unassumingly skeptical of her own work"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400477648">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unattainable manner or to an unattainable degree; "this house is unattainably expensive"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400477834">
	<b:glossaryEntry>suddenly and unexpectedly; "rain caught them unawares"; "sorrow comes to all, and to the young it comes with bittered agony because it takes them unawares"- A.Lincoln</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478037">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without forethought or plan; inadvertently; "came upon the diamond unawares"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478150"
	 b:glossaryEntry='to an unbearable degree; "it was unbearably hot in theroom"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478266">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[without someone''s knowledge; "unbeknownst to me, she made all the arrangements"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478397">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without blushing; "his principal opponent unblushingly declared victory before the ballots had been counted"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478565"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an uncanny manner; "uncannily human robots"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478667"
	 b:glossaryEntry='showing lack of certainty; "he paused uncertainly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400478775">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unchivalrous and ungallant manner; "unchivalrously, the husbands who had to provide such innocent indulgences eventually began to count the costs"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479006">
	<b:glossaryEntry>exceptionally; "a common remedy is uncommonly difficult to find"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479127"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an uncompromising manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479217"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an undesirable manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479299"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an unwanted manner; "he was unwantedly friendly"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479439"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an unusual manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479516">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unconcerned manner; "war was breaking out in Europe, but she unconcernedly planned for a holiday"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479679"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in an uncontrolled manner; "she laughed uncontrollably"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479795">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an uncouth manner; "uncouthly, he told stories that made everybody at the table wince"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400479940"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an unctuous manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480077">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to an undeniable degree or in an undeniable manner; "she is undeniably the most gifted student in the class"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480242"
	 b:glossaryEntry='further down; "see under for further discussion"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480332"
	 b:glossaryEntry='down below; "get under quickly!"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480398"
	 b:glossaryEntry='below the horizon; "the sun went under"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480471"
	 b:glossaryEntry='below some quantity or limit; "fifty dollars or under"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480559">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in or into a state of subordination or subjugation; "we must keep our disappointment under"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480684">
	<b:glossaryEntry>down to defeat, death, or ruin; "the competitiors went under"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480779"
	 b:glossaryEntry='into unconsciousness; "this will put the patient under"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480868">
	<b:glossaryEntry>through a range downward; "children six and under will be admitted free"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400480974">
	<b:glossaryEntry xml:space='preserve'><![CDATA[with the hand swung below shoulder level''; "throwing a ball underarm"]]></b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481092">
	<b:glossaryEntry>beneath the surface of the earth; "water flowing underground"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481193">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in or into hiding or secret operation; "the organization was driven underground"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481313">
	<b:glossaryEntry>slyly and secretly; "Mean revenge, committed underhand"- John Donne; "oldline aristocratic diplomats underhandedly undermined the attempt...to align Germany with the Western democracies"- C.G.Bowers</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481565">
	<b:glossaryEntry>under or below an object or a surface; "we could see the original painting underneath"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481690">
	<b:glossaryEntry>beneath by way of support; "a house with a good foundation underneath"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481799"
	 b:glossaryEntry='lower down on the page; "diagrams with figures underneath"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400481896">
	<b:glossaryEntry>on he lower or downward side; "a chest of drawers all scratched underneath"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482010">
	<b:glossaryEntry>to an undue degree; "she was unduly pessimistic about her future"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482128">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an uneventful manner; "the space shuttle landed uneventfully"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482251">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an ungrammatical manner; "this child speaks ungrammatically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482394">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in a grammatical manner; "this child already speaks grammatically"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482538"
	 b:glossaryEntry="to an unimaginable extent"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482654">
	<b:glossaryEntry>without interruption; "this pleasant state of affairs had continued peacefully and uninterruptedly for many years"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400482830">
	<b:glossaryEntry>in an unnatural way; "his other arm lay across his chest, unnaturally, as if placed there deliberately, for a purpose"</b:glossaryEntry>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400483024"
	 b:glossaryEntry='in a natural or normal manner; "speak naturally and easily"'/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400483139"
	 b:glossaryEntry="with precedent"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400483231"
	 b:glossaryEntry="in an unprecedented manner"/>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="&a;400483337">
